NAME
       cap_get, cap_drop - capabilities

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       uint64_t cervus_cap_get(void);
       int      cervus_cap_drop(uint64_t mask);

DESCRIPTION
       Each task carries a capability mask that gates the privileged
       syscalls: raw device access, I/O ports, rebooting and the like.

       cap_drop clears bits and can never set them, so a program may
       give up what it does not need and cannot take it back. Dropping
       before handling untrusted input limits what a bug can reach.

       Capabilities are inherited across fork and execve.

RETURN VALUE
       The mask, or 0 on success and negative on failure.

SEE ALSO
       auth(2), ioport(2), getpid(2)
